From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: enable module loader net_admin tunable

Qualcomm platforms preload qrtr and qrtr_smd from modules-load.d so the
QRTR transport is available early for dependent services such as audio.
The modules register PF_QIPCRTR during initialization, which requires
CAP_NET_ADMIN.

Enable the upstream kernel_module_load_net_admin tunable by default for
Qualcomm builds. Without it, systemd-modules-load fails to insert the
modules under SELinux enforcing and they are only loaded later through
modalias autoloading.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Qualcomm platform configuration]

Signed-off-by: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 policy/modules/kernel/kernel.te | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/policy/modules/kernel/kernel.te b/policy/modules/kernel/kernel.te
index 648b92ec1..d59aad9c8 100644
--- a/policy/modules/kernel/kernel.te
+++ b/policy/modules/kernel/kernel.te
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ gen_bool(secure_mode_insmod, false)
 ## capability during module initialization.
 ## </p>
 ## </desc>
-gen_tunable(kernel_module_load_net_admin, false)
+gen_tunable(kernel_module_load_net_admin, true)
 
 # assertion related attributes
 attribute can_load_kernmodule;
-- 
2.43.0

